  "unit": "Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Cancelling incorrectly</strong><br/>\n   - Wrong: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n   - Correct: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Losing solutions when multiplying/dividing by a variable</strong><br/>\n   - If you multiply or divide by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, always check <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>â‰ </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Forgetting to distribute negatives</strong><br/>\n   - <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>âˆ’</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, not <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>âˆ’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Square root mistake</strong><br/>\n   - <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></math>, not <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> </p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr/>\n<h3>Inverse operations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Addition â†” Subtraction  </li>\n<li>Multiplication â†” Division  </li>\n<li>Squaring â†” Square root  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math> </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>â‡’</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<h3>Balancing equations</h3>\n<p>What you do to one side, do to the other.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h3>Distribute and Combine</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand parentheses and combine like terms.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>âˆ’</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math> </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>âˆ’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>â‡’</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>â‡’</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<h3>Fractions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Multiply through by least common denominator (LCD).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math><br/>\nMultiply both sides by 15:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>â‡’</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<h3>Decimals</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Multiply through by powers of 10 to clear decimals.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\nMultiply through by 10:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>â‡’</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr/>\n<ul>\n<li>Always simplify before solving.  </li>\n<li>Eliminate fractions and decimals early.  </li>\n<li>Plug solution back to check (some SAT questions have “extraneous solutions”).  </li>\n<li>Watch for absolute values, square roots, and restrictions.  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n3) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) Simplify: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> </p>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> (for <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>â‰ </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>)</p>\n\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n1) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n2) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n3) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n\n4) Solve: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<br />\n4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>â‡’</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n\n5) Simplify: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> \n<br />\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> (for <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>â‰ </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>)",
